Chapter: BvtPlayDoors
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtNpcMove
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 D-7a: a play actor's walk opens a door through the town doors as any walker does, and the walk's packets reach the
 door sync, so the door closes itself. On BvtNpcMove's fixture door 0 is opened as a walker opens it. Answers a bit per
 check: 1 the door opened, 2 no autoclose timer from the open alone, 4 none after the no-play default hook, 8 one after
 the composite's plays hook; -1 to -3 a fixture that failed.
  pdx-armed : CompositeGame -> Boolean
  pdx-armed (owner) = wtm-find owner.timers wd-door-timer 0 >= 0
  pdx-run : CompositeGame -> Integer
  pdx-run (owner) = when owner.town-doors
    is None -> -1
    is Just (doors) -> if wd-locked doors 0 | bit-and (peek-byte doors.opened 0) 1 /= 0 then -2
      else when wd-toggle doors owner.checkpoint.game 0
        is Err (_) -> -3
        is Ok (reply) -> let opened = if bit-and (peek-byte doors.opened 0) 1 /= 0 then 1 else 0
          in let unarmed = if pdx-armed owner then 0 else 2
          in let none = plr-doors-none reply.packets
          in let still = if pdx-armed owner then 0 else 4
          in let synced = owner.plays.doors reply.packets
          in let armed = if pdx-armed owner then 8 else 0
          in opened + unarmed + still + armed
  bvt-play-doors : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-play-doors (unused) = when bnm-founded 0
    is Err (e) -> bvt-check ("play doors fixture: " & e) False
    is Ok (owner) -> act
      n <- pdx-run owner
      a <- bvt-check ("D-7a: a door a play actor's walk opens arms its autoclose through the plays hook (code " & show n & ")") (n == 15)
      a
    end
